coder › Implemented `wrap(text, width)` and added tests, on branch `implement-wrap` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/wrap.ts` — implemented `wrap`: splits input on newlines; a blank/whitespace-only line separates paragraphs, consecutive blank lines collapse, output paragraphs joined with a single `\n\n`. Within a paragraph lines are split on `[ \t]+` (empty tokens dropped, so space runs collapse to one), words packed greedily up to `width`, words longer than `width` split across lines (filling the remainder of the current line first). Lines are joined with single spaces so none ends in a space. `width < 1` (including `0`, negatives, `NaN`) throws `RangeError`.
- `src/wrap.test.ts` — 14 tests covering: breaking/packing, space collapsing, long-word splitting (standalone and mid-line), one blank line kept / multiple collapsed, single newline joined with space, no trailing spaces + line lengths, empty input, width 1, `RangeError` for widths 0/-1/-100.

